  "descriptions": {
    "preferred": "'Hiu\\ga yama' is reportedly a seedling selection of 'Nomura', one of the oldest known cultivars. The leaf lobes are longer and more slender than are those of 'Nomura' The color in the early season is a deep purple red which becomes less intense as the season progresses. By late summer it is greenish bronze-purple. The leaves are of growth habit rather erect. This cultivar is not widely grown, probably because it has no outstandingly different features from many other red cultivars. The name has been variously spelled"
  },
